 The supplied Blender package now composes a local service under the actual centralized BaseConnector: 200 named catalog actions plus 3 scoped bridge/job tools. Existing ToolRegistry policy and exact host approvals remain required, with per-instance scope binding, deterministic explicit Blender commands, small category/query discovery, independent provider persistence, bounded job observation and no mutation replay. The bundled Blender guide enters existing SkillMemory as untrusted capability guidance, not permission. Scene metadata cannot authorize Python or add-ons. The active MCP config is unchanged: enabling this write-capable integration is pending explicit approval following automatic review rejection.
